        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c3d12196-9929-5fbd-aadd-10581a1d3b20",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Punisher: The Album\n- Companies: Wind-up Records\n- People: Amy Lee\n- Organizations: Seether, Evanescence, Drowning Pool, Edgewater\n- Places: Dallas, Texas\n- Concepts: lead singles, music videos, soundtrack albums, band names\n\nFacts:\n- Drowning Pool is an American rock band that formed in Dallas, Texas in 1996.\n- Drowning Pool was named after the film \"The Drowning Pool.\"\n- The Punisher: The Album is the official soundtrack album for the film \"The Punisher,\" and Wind-up Records released it in 2004.\n- The lead singles from The Punisher: The Album were \"Broken\" by Seether and Amy Lee, \"Step Up\" by Drowning Pool, and \"Eyes Wired Shut\" by Edgewater.\n- \"Broken,\" \"Step Up,\" and \"Eyes Wired Shut\" each have accompanying music videos.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
